    {
      "name": "DecryptPEMBlock",
      "summary": "DecryptPEMBlock takes a PEM block encrypted according to RFC 1423 and the password used to encrypt it and returns a slice of decrypted DER encoded bytes. It inspects the DEK-Info header to determine the algorithm used for decryption. If no DEK-Info header is present, an error is returned. If an incorrect password is detected an [IncorrectPasswordError] is returned. Because of deficiencies in the format, it's not always possible to detect an incorrect password. In these cases no error will be returned but the decrypted DER bytes will be random noise.",
      "signature": "func DecryptPEMBlock(b *pem.Block, password []byte) ([]byte, error)",
      "params": [
